  <!-- ==================== METHODOLOGY ==================== -->
  <section class="lio-lp-review__methodology">
    <div class="lio-lp-review__wrap">
      <h2>Our testing methodology</h2>
      <p>We evaluated each flavored air device across six criteria: <strong>Ritual Fidelity</strong> (how closely the hand-to-mouth + breath + flavor loop matches a real vape or cigarette pull), <strong>Flavor Experience</strong> (natural vs. artificial, potency, variety), <strong>Portability &amp; Social Use</strong> (can you use it on a plane, in an office, at dinner without drawing attention), <strong>Build Quality</strong> (materials, feel, durability), <strong>Ease of Use</strong> (setup time, refill/core swapping, maintenance), and <strong>Value</strong> (total cost over 90 days including device and refills). Each device was used daily by three testers — a current vaper, a former smoker, and a nail-biter trying to stop — for the full 8-week test window.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== #1 LIO ==================== -->
  <article class="lio-lp-review__pick">
    <div class="lio-lp-review__wrap">
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-header">
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-rank">#1 Best Overall</span>
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-score">9.6<span>/10</span></span>
      </div>
      <h2>Lio® — The Original Flavored Air Device</h2>
      <p class="lio-lp-review__pick-best-for">Best for: Anyone serious about breaking a ritual-based habit &mdash; vapers, smokers, and behavioral fidgeters &mdash; who want a real device, not a disposable gimmick.</p>
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-grid">
        <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-img-wrap">
          <img src="{{ hero_device_img }}?width=1000"
               alt="Lio handcrafted olive wood flavored air device"
               class="lio-lp-review__pick-img"
               width="1000" height="1000"
               loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Lio dominated our testing on every dimension that actually matters. The handcrafted olive or walnut wood body feels substantial in the hand &mdash; not like a cheap plastic throwaway. The natural aroma core system is the most elegant refill solution in the category: open the pouch, fray the cotton core, insert, breathe. No drip, no wick saturation, no pod alignment, no battery indicator to decode.</p>
          <p>The behavioral loop replication is the real story. Because Lio is pulled through the same airflow draw you&rsquo;d use on a vape or cigarette, and because the natural plant-based flavor hits your olfactory system at the exact moment of inhalation, your brain registers the full ritual &mdash; hand, breath, flavor, relief &mdash; without a single milligram of nicotine. Our vaping tester reported a measurable reduction in pull-count within the first week. By week 4, he was down over 70% from baseline.</p>
          <p>The three-tier device lineup &mdash; Original (fixed airflow), Plus (adjustable airflow), Pro (adjustable airflow + magnetic fidgeting) &mdash; is unique in the category and lets you pick the level of physical engagement that matches your habit. Nail-biters and anxious fidgeters gravitate to the Pro. Former smokers tend to prefer the Plus for a tighter, firmer pull.</p>
          <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-proscons">
            <strong>Pros</strong>
            <p class="lio-lp-review__pros">Handcrafted wood (olive or walnut) · Natural plant-based aroma cores · Three device tiers including magnetic fidget Pro · No battery, no vapor, no smell · Works anywhere — plane, office, restaurant · 150,000+ users · 1,000+ 5-star reviews · Clean-label ingredients</p>
            <strong>Cons</strong>
            <p class="lio-lp-review__cons">Premium price point vs. disposable alternatives · Subtle flavor (users expecting vape-strength flavor may need a few days to adjust)</p>
          </div>
          <a href="{{ primary_cta_url }}" class="lio-lp-review__inline-cta">
            {%- if journey_pack and journey_pack.available -%}
              Start Your Lio Journey — {{ journey_pack.price | money }}
            {%- else -%}
              Start Your Lio Journey — €39
            {%- endif -%}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ==================== #2 CAPNOS ==================== -->
  <article class="lio-lp-review__pick">
    <div class="lio-lp-review__wrap">
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-header">
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-rank">#2 Runner-up</span>
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-score">8.4<span>/10</span></span>
      </div>
      <h2>Capnos</h2>
      <p class="lio-lp-review__pick-best-for">Best for: Former vapers who specifically miss the &ldquo;throat hit&rdquo; &mdash; the pressurized pop on inhale &mdash; more than the flavor.</p>
      <p>Capnos built its brand around a silicone valve that pops open under inhale pressure, delivering a pressurized &ldquo;throat hit&rdquo; sensation that genuinely does feel closer to a real vape pull than Lio&rsquo;s softer airflow. For heavy vapers who miss the physical pressure of a draw, this is a legitimate differentiator.</p>
      <p>However, flavor on Capnos is an afterthought. The base models ship flavorless, with optional essential oil drops on a replaceable cotton wick inside the device. The flavor experience is subtle at best and fiddly to maintain &mdash; drop, wait, inhale, re-drop every few weeks. Compared to Lio&rsquo;s clean pre-saturated plug-and-play cores, Capnos feels like a 2015 vape mod in a category that has moved on.</p>
      <p>Build quality on the premium Legura and BRE-Z is solid (aluminum body, fidget crown), but the budget Zero and E-Z models are plastic and feel disposable. And some testers found the audible &ldquo;pop&rdquo; of the silicone valve embarrassing in quiet public settings.</p>
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-proscons">
        <strong>Pros</strong>
        <p class="lio-lp-review__pros">Strongest throat-hit sensation in the category · Premium Legura has fidget crown · Reusable one-time-purchase design</p>
        <strong>Cons</strong>
        <p class="lio-lp-review__cons">Flavor is weak and requires drip-wick setup · Audible &ldquo;pop&rdquo; on every inhale · Budget models feel cheap · Flavor variety limited to essential oil drops</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ==================== #3 MOXĒ ==================== -->
  <article class="lio-lp-review__pick">
    <div class="lio-lp-review__wrap">
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-header">
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-rank">#3</span>
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-score">7.9<span>/10</span></span>
      </div>
      <h2>MOXĒ</h2>
      <p>MOXĒ makes clean, simple essential-oil-based twist-and-inhale pens that work. They&rsquo;re honest about what they are &mdash; aromatherapy inhalers, not habit-replacement devices &mdash; and the Made in USA positioning appeals to wellness buyers. Flavors are limited to mint and essential oil blends (Spearmint, Menthol, Wintermint, Cinnamint, Peppermint Mocha), and each pen lasts about 30 days.</p>
      <p>The downside: MOXĒ is a single-use pen. When it&rsquo;s done, you throw it away and buy another. There&rsquo;s no reusable device, no fidget element, and no adjustable airflow. For someone with a serious ritual-based habit, this is a lightweight solution. Great for a mild oral fixation &mdash; insufficient for a 30-year pack-a-day smoker.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- ==================== #4 CIGTRUS ==================== -->
  <article class="lio-lp-review__pick">
    <div class="lio-lp-review__wrap">
      <div class="lio-lp-review__pick-header">
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-rank">#4 Budget</span>
        <span class="lio-lp-review__pick-score">7.5<span>/10</span></span>
      </div>
      <h2>Cigtrus</h2>
      <p>Cigtrus is the pharmacy play in this category: cheap, disposable, citrus-mint aromatherapy inhalers sold in 3-packs and 20-packs. At roughly $10 for a 3-pack, it&rsquo;s the budget pick. The flavor is strong citrus-mint (almost medicinal), and the disposable plastic design makes it easy to carry.</p>
      <p>It works &mdash; for a few days. Then you throw it out. This is the category&rsquo;s lowest-effort solution, and it shows. No device tiers, no core system, no community, no fidget engagement. If you&rsquo;re testing whether a flavored air device concept works for you before committing, Cigtrus is a reasonable $10 experiment. If you&rsquo;re trying to actually break a habit, you&rsquo;ll outgrow it in a week.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

